WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.437
Now the sensitive part.

2
00:00:01.437 --> 00:00:06.201
Issue and Manage Certificates is
the AD CS certificate-manager right.

3
00:00:06.201 --> 00:00:08.971
Microsoft says it lets
the holder issue, deny,

4
00:00:08.971 --> 00:00:13.838
revoke and reinstate certificates
without the broader Manage CA permission.

5
00:00:13.838 --> 00:00:19.226
Defender for Identity's ESC7 assessment
flags unprivileged holders of it.

6
00:00:19.226 --> 00:00:24.113
Here's the first correction to the
Federal Modernization Workbook's Book 07.

7
00:00:24.113 --> 00:00:28.322
Chapter 05 says the program scopes
the account to the templates

8
00:00:28.322 --> 00:00:32.451
the platform is meant to issue, as
if the CA had a control for that.

9
00:00:32.451 --> 00:00:37.697
Microsoft's current guidance says to define
each certificate manager's templates and

10
00:00:37.697 --> 00:00:41.705
requesters and to run positive
and negative authorization tests,

11
00:00:41.705 --> 00:00:46.660
but it also says Microsoft Learn doesn't
publish a Windows Server 2025 step-by-step

12
00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:50.523
procedure for configuring
certificate-manager restrictions,

13
00:00:50.523 --> 00:00:53.875
and to validate any existing
restriction in a lab first.

14
00:00:53.875 --> 00:00:56.595
So the scoping rests on
template permissions,

15
00:00:56.595 --> 00:00:59.888
plus allowed and denied test
requests proven in the lab.

16
00:00:59.888 --> 00:01:03.413
Book 07 has been updated
to match to say so.

17
00:01:03.413 --> 00:01:05.480
My inference about why that matters:

18
00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:08.788
template permissions limit
what the account can request.

19
00:01:08.788 --> 00:01:11.840
They don't narrow the
certificate-manager right itself,

20
00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:15.225
which is why the negative test
and the alerts carry the weight.

21
00:01:15.225 --> 00:01:18.200
The program's controls,
as design guidance.

22
00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:21.474
A dedicated account, a group
managed service account

23
00:01:21.474 --> 00:01:24.450
where the CA allows it,
denied interactive logon.

24
00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:28.550
DCOM to the CA allowed only from
the platform's engine servers.

25
00:01:28.550 --> 00:01:31.725
Read and Enroll only on
the platform's templates.

26
00:01:31.725 --> 00:01:37.432
Alerts on event 4887 when this
requester gets a certificate

27
00:01:37.432 --> 00:01:42.112
outside those templates,
and on 4882, 4890 and 4892.

28
00:01:42.112 --> 00:01:45.627
And the account goes into
the quarterly ESC7 review,

29
00:01:45.627 --> 00:01:48.325
with the negative test result on record.

30
00:01:48.325 --> 00:01:54.434
Sources: Microsoft Learn, Secure, delegate
and audit a certification authority;

31
00:01:54.434 --> 00:01:58.506
Review and dispose of
pending certificate requests;

32
00:01:58.506 --> 00:02:02.949
Defender for Identity
certificate posture assessments;

33
00:02:02.949 --> 00:02:08.687
CyberArk 26.1 Microsoft ADCS CA template
and Securing credential objects;

34
00:02:08.687 --> 00:02:13.560
Book 07, Chapter 03 (ESC7) and
Chapter 05 (four permission systems).
